**Read:** [Chemical Reactor Analysis and Design Fundamentals — Rawlings and Ekerdt](../sources/Chemical-Reactor-Analysis-Rawlings-Ekerdt.lingua#r_7YQAV27Y3J0B537Z6K5HDN8H0A), the complete reaction-rate and parameter-estimation chapters with substantial problems; [Chemical and Biological Reaction Engineering — MIT 10.37](../sources/Reaction-Engineering-MIT-10-37.lingua#r_67AEXD9K1DJ46SV942PAZHZ4BZ), the whole mechanism/rate-law teaching and assignments; [Graduate Numerical Methods Applied to Chemical Engineering — MIT 10.34](../sources/Graduate-Numerical-Methods-MIT-10-34.lingua#r_1NTDP6EFQGR8HWP34VT9ZJ98DV), the full relevant least-squares, nonlinear-system and error-analysis work.

A rate law relates a specified chemical production/consumption rate to state variables and parameters. Its basis matters: amount per reactor volume, mass of catalyst, accessible area or active sites are different quantities. An empirical power law is not automatically an elementary reaction or a mechanism.

Derive the connection between the observed signal and the species balance. Sampling/quenching, detector calibration, finite mixing, changing density and temperature histories can influence the inferred rate. Differentiating noisy concentrations can amplify error; fitting an integrated model introduces its own assumptions and numerical questions.

Compare alternative mechanisms, parameter correlations and the experimental domain. A small fitting residual does not prove identifiability or predictive ability. Arrhenius parameters can compensate for one another over a narrow temperature interval, while a changed phase or transport regime can alter apparent activation behavior.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete primary kinetic study with its method and data provenance. Fit or independently reproduce the central parameters, test residuals/uncertainty and hold out a meaningful changed condition. Explain which experiment would discriminate a competing mechanism and whether the published measurements can identify the claimed parameters. Preserve failures as evidence for revising the model.

**Continue:** [Relate catalysis to pathways, selectivity, and equilibrium constraints](../../general-chemistry/kinetics/Catalysis-and-competing-pathways.lingua#r_4Z85MENW43NS707PTCHNTDTDME).

